  "findings": [
    "Soul is the independent red normal-attack / blue skill system; no retired DragonSoul content is restored.",
    "Packed socket2 = charge minutes * 10000 + remaining strikes; socket1 marks active; affect SP cost stores instance ID.",
    "Owned timer adds one minute-unit per 60 real seconds (5 seconds on test_server). No offline recharge was found in these paths.",
    "Activation requires at least 60 charge units and positive strikes. Same-color activation replaces the prior instance; new owner must serialize explicit deactivate/activate atomically.",
    "PvE player attacks only, not while polymorphed. Three charge tiers use value3/4/5 divided by 10 as a total damage multiplier.",
    "At strike exhaustion old code subtracts 60 charge units, resets strikes from value2 and disables below 60. New state has distinct typed fields, no decimal packing or float damage.",
    "Raw scroll refinement consumes one scroll on both outcomes and creates a fresh target prototype on success. New plan retains ItemKey/instance and increments level with explicit initial Soul-state reset.",
    "Source core value1 contains 1..5 across each five-row refinement chain. Exact semantics/target level relation require reviewed offline mapping, never runtime ID/name arithmetic.",
    "value0==1 can bypass the old timer capacity stop. The 10 captured cores all use value0==0; uncapped variants are not silently converted.",
    "The current raw refine path checks generic tuning subtype but not Soul scroll discriminator/type again. New domain requires exact published core/scroll kinds.",
    "Source use can refuse toggling off when charge/strikes are invalid. The new deactivate path permits retired/policy-changed cleanup for structurally valid state.",
    "New owner must bind stable damage-event/target identity, serialize one debit per committed damage and reconcile durable operation ID on CommitUnknown.",
    "Zero damage is rejected without debit; exact integer rounding replaces floating-point drift. These are explicit hardening differences, not a live combat rewrite."
  ],
